{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded","id":76114,"title":"Storms and the Dragon-Blooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-20T22:59:49-08:00","id":76114,"title":"Storms and the Dragon-Blooded","content":"So, I'm currently sitting at my house at 1:45am in the middle of a pretty grand storm. The worst that I've had this year, at the very least. Plenty of rain being pushed passed faster than my eye can really follow, the wind howling like crazy, lightning flashing every few seconds with zero time between light and sound so I'm figuring its right above my house, all mixed with the slight suspicion that that big tree further up the hill is finally going to be blown over and crash into the house.<br /> <br /> Is this what it's like to be near a pissed off Air Dragon Blood? :.D<br /> <br /> Or any DB really. The anxiety that at any moment that elemental fury is going to be unleashed and terror unleashed upon you and those around you? And then your 'solar' buddy reeaally f***s up and starts a fight. Every blow a crack of thunder right over head...will the collateral smack into you? Flashes of light and essence blind you for moments as you feel those peels of thunder reverberate through your chest? And that god awful sound of their anima, like the wind during a hurricane, that pressure that almost blows you off your feet?<br /> <br /> Then, it all calms down...a standstill. Your Solar friend talking a brief moment of philosophy with him...the eye of the storm. But you feel your friend saying the wrong thing...its building back up... maybe it was the calm, or maybe it just really is now, but its all the more furious for it. A gale, a crash, another blinding flash and for a brief moment, you wonder...<br /> <br /> How the hell do you fight a storm?<br /> <br /> <br /> In conclusion, Dragon-Blooded are freaking awesome for evoking such imagery....and Solars are also incredible for being able to wrestle it.<br /> <br /> (And this thread is just something to take my mind off the elements raging above and around my head.)<br /> <br /> [Edit: And for all you Deathlords out there...should I die tonight, whether by being crushed by the house or dropped by a tornado or any other crazy and unfortunate circumstance...or any circumstance at all, mind... I WILL take the deal. I promise.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":697,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","user":"Arteliex","date":". 02-21-2014, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T23:10:24-08:00","id":76117,"title":"","content":"Dragonblooded are not nearly powerful enough for that kind of thing. I know it's just imagery but an anima banner isn't a storm. Also Dragonblooded are elemental soldiers, not just about elements, so the stuff they have is more like a sword that crackles with lightning or fists that are on fire but don't burn, ect.<br /> <br /> Now what might work with this is an awesome powerful storm exigent from the next edition. That'd be pretty rocking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T23:20:43-08:00","id":76120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76117#post76117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragonblooded are not nearly powerful enough for that kind of thing. I know it's just imagery but an anima banner isn't a storm. Also Dragonblooded are elemental soldiers, not just about elements, so the stuff they have is more like a sword that crackles with lightning or fists that are on fire but don't burn, ect.<br /> <br /> Now what might work with this is an awesome powerful storm exigent from the next edition. That'd be pretty rocking.</div> </div> </div> </div>DB player: I want my air anima to be a raging storm around me.<br /> Bad ST: No. Something cool like that is for exigents.<br /> <br /> DB player: I want my air anima to be a raging storm around me.<br /> Good ST: You can do that but it's something your PC has to develop. *thinks, 'Good thing I have that exigent book to help me create a super anima.'*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":296,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","user":"hippokrene","date":". 02-21-2014, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T23:27:59-08:00","id":76122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76120#post76120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> DB player: I want my air anima to be a raging storm around me.<br /> Bad ST: No. Something cool like that is for exigents.<br /> <br /> DB player: I want my air anima to be a raging storm around me.<br /> Good ST: You can do that but it's something your PC has to develop. *thinks, 'Good thing I have that exigent book to help me create a super anima.'*</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I'm just saying that it's out of theme and out of scale for standard DBs. An entire storm is way too large of an effect, even for a charm, and DBs tend much more to lead toward direct martial things with some elemental themes or enhancements rather than das-\u00fcberstorm.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly legit to develop though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T23:28:05-08:00","id":76123,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid I disagree with you pretty hard on that.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded anima banner actively harms the environment that they're in. Anyone who get's too close gets damaged, depending on which stage the Anima Banner is at. Their expressions of Elemental Bolt and Burst, mixed with their flaring anima can definitely be extremely flashy... Lightning bolts that explode, Fire bursting from the ground... And that's not even touching yet the Dragon-Vortex-esque effects of later levels.<br /> <br /> Specifically, though, my mind was on the Air-Dragon blooded. Wind actively whips around them constantly unless they consciously surpress it, and its stronger for Higher Essence and Breeding Dragon-Bloods. If they get enraged, and their Anima starts flaring to boot, it seems like it really would feel like a storm around you, and I don't think it would be less dramatic for other Dragon-Blooded Aspects either.<br /> <br /> And I think that's really thematic. They aren't perfectly in tune with their Elemental Nature, as evidenced by a Peripheral Essence pool. So it lets loose and destroys, and in a very obvious way. It's scary. It's awesome. And it makes them seem extremely powerful since they're the controllers of this awesome power.<br /> <br /> Now of course, I'm not saying that just when they're fighting that their anima makes the sky grow dark, hurricane force winds erupt, lightning flashes, trees grow, boulder fall, volcanoes erupt, etc, etc... I'm just saying it FEELS like it is to those nearby. Of all the Exalts, I'd say that the Dragon-Bloods FEEL more like the atom bombs that all Exalts are. Buuut, I understand if others feel differently...just I hate the mass DB hate, like anything that makes them awesome that doesn't involve teamwork needs to be shot down...and now I'm rambling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T23:48:08-08:00","id":76125,"title":"","content":"Dragon Vortex Attack has always been a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T00:11:28-08:00","id":76128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76123#post76123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now of course, I'm not saying that just when they're fighting that their anima makes the sky grow dark, hurricane force winds erupt, lightning flashes, trees grow, boulder fall, volcanoes erupt, etc, etc... I'm just saying it FEELS like it is to those nearby. Of all the Exalts, I'd say that the Dragon-Bloods FEEL more like the atom bombs that all Exalts are. Buuut, I understand if others feel differently...just I hate the mass DB hate, like anything that makes them awesome that doesn't involve teamwork needs to be shot down...and now I'm rambling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhh okay sorry my apologies. I thought you meant like when they fight they draw in clouds and massive winds over a big area. Even Dragon Vortex Attack pales in comparison to an actual storm.<br /> <br /> I'm actually pretty sure that celestial exalted can have big noises and stuff in their animas as well, so a fight between them might have the whistling of the wind drowned out by the roar of a golden tiger. Rather than just have all of the effects come from the DB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T00:57:36-08:00","id":76134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76117#post76117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragonblooded are not nearly powerful enough for that kind of thing. I know it's just imagery but an anima banner isn't a storm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dragon Blooded anima basically is a storm, including how it damages things in direct contact with it.<br /> <br /> Don't forget that an anima banner at the higher levels of its power is visible for miles. Given the elemental and physical nature of the Dragon Blooded one, this could easily mean that a Terrestrial who is going all out causes buffeting weather effects across the county, particularly if their Essence is strong (even if the damaging flux only occurs within a few feet).<br /> <br /> The Aspect markings of Air also include little wind effects, that are stronger based on age, breeding and Essence, and can get violent to reflect the Exalt's mood.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T01:23:01-08:00","id":76140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76134#post76134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Dragon Blooded anima basically is a storm, including how it damages things in direct contact with it.<br /> <br /> Don't forget that an anima banner at the higher levels of its power is visible for miles. Given the elemental and physical nature of the Dragon Blooded one, this could easily mean that a Terrestrial who is going all out causes buffeting weather effects across the county, particularly if their Essence is strong (even if the damaging flux only occurs within a few feet).<br /> <br /> The Aspect markings of Air also include little wind effects, that are stronger based on age, breeding and Essence, and can get violent to reflect the Exalt's mood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly thinking something like this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6IJnn63XEmk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6IJnn63XEmk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6IJnn63XEmk\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6IJnn63XEmk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which blows even Dragon Vortex out of the water when it comes to scope, size wise at the very least.<br /> <br /> As to anima affecting a whole countryside, even though the flux only does damage in a small area...I just can't see it. It might just be personal preference I guess but even a windstorm whipping through a town is a bit big for all but the most powerful Dragonblooded. I might be able to see it if a bunch of air aspects all got together and started doing crazy shit, then it might start to summon some cloud cover maybe and have the winds extend out to a larger area.<br /> <br /> I think my problem is that if an essence 4 charm only goes out 200 yards, and that's a specifically wide area war charm, then things that are smaller essence requirements and cost should be much more localized. Not to mention the other aspects can't really do that. Fire and water especially need to stay within the flux radius, and even then it gets silly at higher essence. Can you imagine a bonfire that's 10 meters wide? That's massive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T06:52:42-08:00","id":76247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76140#post76140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was mostly thinking something like this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6IJnn63XEmk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6IJnn63XEmk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6IJnn63XEmk\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6IJnn63XEmk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that seems pretty much right for air anima at the highest levels. It's an impressive and powerful display, visible for miles, punctuated by fierce, damaging localized events. Assume your Air Aspect is fighting some sort of very mobile being that doesn't produce its own anima (say, one or more Agata) and you can account for the fact there's no other display and the lightning strikes are occurring in different places across the city. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76140#post76140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my problem is that if an essence 4 charm only goes out 200 yards, and that's a specifically wide area war charm, then things that are smaller essence requirements and cost should be much more localized.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but look at what Dragon Vortex actually does. Most people caught in it's area will be killed immediately, even a healthy portion of unprotected heroes would be soundly incapacitated and die off within five seconds of exposure. It's not the sort of effect that leads to awed laughter and videos on youtube. The anima banner, on the other hand, is much more sound and fury than actual damaging force. The thunder and the rain here are not having any pronounced effect. They're certainly not killing people outright. It's all just about providing an atmospheric backdrop to the action.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76140#post76140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention the other aspects can't really do that. Fire and water especially need to stay within the flux radius, and even then it gets silly at higher essence. Can you imagine a bonfire that's 10 meters wide? That's massive.</div> </div> </div> </div>It gets a lot easier to handle if you remember that the anima doesn't just have to be a solid chunk of the element, and that the anima display and the elemental flux area don't have to be the same. A powerful fire aspect could just as easily be shedding a field of dancing, floating embers accross a wide area with a flux zone that's not even visible except for the fact things start to smolder when he steps too close. I had a water aspect in one of my games who produced a low, ground-clinging fog as an anima display and who visibly (and shockingly on a few occasions) drew the water out of nearby objects and people into his skin for flux damage. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T08:21:05-08:00","id":76285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76140#post76140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to anima affecting a whole countryside, even though the flux only does damage in a small area...I just can't see it. It might just be personal preference I guess but even a windstorm whipping through a town is a bit big for all but the most powerful Dragonblooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a cosmetic effect, and the basic model for all fully unveiled anima banners.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fire and water especially need to stay within the flux radius</div> </div> </div> </div>Fire is super easy because it generates light (and a bit of relatively mild heat).<br /> <br /> Water can probably also have a bit of storming, or possibly just fog.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you imagine a bonfire that's 10 meters wide? That's massive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you familiar with how the people of the Britain and Ireland are so fond of bonfires that they basically made up an excuse to include them in holidays for other things, and then forgot what those other things were because they really just wanted the bonfires?<br /> <br /> I've seen bonfires that were literally bigger than my house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T11:19:36-08:00","id":76436,"title":"","content":"Well, yes. I believe you've mentioned you live in Ireland before, Isator. I've had the chance to visit there in the past, near County Cork, and it's beautiful, but damn it's cold. I'd want one too.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, I've never seen an issue with massive anima banners. I mean, look at what they have for <i>visibility</i> at the highest Peripheral. You can see a Solar's anima banner for <i>miles</i> when they flare, and that's a massive column of light and displays of power. Why not the same for the Terrestrials?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T11:33:06-08:00","id":76448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76436#post76436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That said, I've never seen an issue with massive anima banners. I mean, look at what they have for <i>visibility</i> at the highest Peripheral. You can see a Solar's anima banner for <i>miles</i> when they flare, and that's a massive column of light and displays of power. Why not the same for the Terrestrials?</div> </div> </div> </div> Just to play devil's advocate, because this miles thing has been mentioned a couple times:<br /> <br /> You know what else can be seen from miles away? The Statue of Liberty. Still, most storms would be tremendously wider, which I think is the greater point of contention. Height is the relevant measure for distance of vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T11:40:13-08:00","id":76455,"title":"","content":".... Why would they be wider? What Charms is the Terrestrial using to augment their anima banner in such a manner as to cause it to engulf such an area?<br /> <br /> The anima banner of the Exalted is a blatantly supernatural effect, localized on them and their surroundings. When a Solar flares up, it's like a massive shaft of daylight and their visual representatives. There's nothing natural about it. When a Sidereal does the same, the stars of their constellations can be seen, even in broad daylight. Still nothing natural about it.<br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is, you're trying to apply weather logic to pure magical displays of force. These are huge representations of not-entirely-controlled power leaking out of their bodies, and affecting the world around them, not normal phenomena.<br /> <br /> Edit: Hell, look at the secondary effects of the Solar banner: It bleaches out all the colors around it, scouring them down to a pure white, among other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":374,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","user":"Nocte ex Mortis","date":". 02-21-2014, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T11:47:28-08:00","id":76465,"title":"","content":"No, I'm suggesting an anima banner WOULDN'T be wider. I'm suggesting that using a storm as an example of an Air anima banner is perhaps not a good example unless you're talking about quite a localized storm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T11:54:34-08:00","id":76469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76436#post76436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I've never seen an issue with massive anima banners. I mean, look at what they have for <i>visibility</i> at the highest Peripheral. You can see a Solar's anima banner for <i>miles</i> when they flare, and that's a massive column of light and displays of power. Why not the same for the Terrestrials?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not really a big issue for me, but it's worth pointing out that if a Solar was lit up even as bright as a regular bonfire, you could totally see him from miles. I'm not really sure this should apply to terrestrials, firstly because some of the terrestrial anima banners, particularly water, end up being some rolling fog accompanied by the crushing silence and dark of the ocean depths. The second reason I think it doesn't really fit is that, while DBs are awesome, they aren't as powerful as the celestial exalted. I don't think the anima banners of the terrestrial exalted should be drastically smaller than the celestial ones, but they shouldn't really be so much bigger.<br /> <br /> Lastly you can get a lot of terrestrials together, certainly way easier than getting a bunch of Solars together. and combining massive anima effects that are so different together feels awkward. Like a massive rainstorm from the air/water guys, while brushfires are breaking out and tremors are shocking through the ground and flowers are blooming and vines growing ect. It just seems too much.<br /> <br /> I will say though that Dragon Vortex attack is bad to base it off of because it's so deadly though. However I'm holding on to the idea that an irish superfire wandering around with a little person inside it is still too much.<br /> <br /> Again it's not a big issue, and if people are having fun with it then by all means go nuts with it, I just think it doesn't fit at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T12:01:47-08:00","id":76471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76448#post76448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just to play devil's advocate, because this miles thing has been mentioned a couple times:<br /> <br /> You know what else can be seen from miles away? The Statue of Liberty. Still, most storms would be tremendously wider, which I think is the greater point of contention. Height is the relevant measure for distance of vision.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to point out that if you're seeing a beam of light (like a solar anima) from a mile away, it's because the spread of light reaches for at least a mile. Even in Creation, light isn't a solid object like a stone pillar.<br /> <br /> The Solar anima isn't just tall, it's also wide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T12:10:14-08:00","id":76475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76471#post76471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to point out that if you're seeing a beam of light (like a solar anima) from a mile away, it's because the spread of light reaches for at least a mile. Even in Creation, light isn't a solid object like a stone pillar.<br /> <br /> The Solar anima isn't just tall, it's also wide.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he was more referencing the crepuscular rays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T12:26:39-08:00","id":76489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76471#post76471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm going to point out that if you're seeing a beam of light (like a solar anima) from a mile away, it's because the spread of light reaches for at least a mile. Even in Creation, light isn't a solid object like a stone pillar. The Solar anima isn't just tall, it's also wide.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're scientifically correct. You see light because it reaches your eye. Still, perceptually, I've seen lights from very far away indeed (many miles) that even close up would not appear to be particularly vast. I don't have to be bathed in the light of a searchlight, nor does it need to be as wide as a storm, for me to be able to see it from miles away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T14:27:42-08:00","id":76580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76465#post76465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm suggesting an anima banner WOULDN'T be wider. I'm suggesting that using a storm as an example of an Air anima banner is perhaps not a good example unless you're talking about quite a localized storm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see, my apologies, I thought you were arguing that the Terrestrial anima should be that massive. I think it should be both localized and massive. There should be no doubts in your mind when two Exalts throw down that Something Terrible is happening. If you can see the displays, you're probably too close (Yes, a mile is too close for comfort in this case.).<br /> <br /> My viewpoint on it is this, and it is kind of a coupout, but at the same time, it's the truth: It's magic. It doesn't fully have to make sense, any moreso than the fact that the Abyssal anima covers things in grave dirt, or a hundred other things, or that the Infernal anima banner can drive someone utterly mad by looking at it.<br /> <br /> What you have is an unleashed display of elemental <i>force</i>. It could be as elaborate as ten thousand shards of ice coming together to coat the ground, and every flat surface, in a perfect sheet, or a raging bonfire erupting upwards in a mushroom cloud, or that for a moment every flower, tree, and plant in the area suddenly bursts into venomous bloom. It's unbridled power from inside the Exalt erupting outwards in displays that are blatantly unnatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T15:04:32-08:00","id":76614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=76580#post76580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I see, my apologies, I thought you were arguing that the Terrestrial anima should be that massive. I think it should be both localized and massive. There should be no doubts in your mind when two Exalts throw down that Something Terrible is happening. If you can see the displays, you're probably too close (Yes, a mile is too close for comfort in this case.).<br /> <br /> My viewpoint on it is this, and it is kind of a coupout, but at the same time, it's the truth: It's magic. It doesn't fully have to make sense, any moreso than the fact that the Abyssal anima covers things in grave dirt, or a hundred other things, or that the Infernal anima banner can drive someone utterly mad by looking at it.<br /> <br /> What you have is an unleashed display of elemental <i>force</i>. It could be as elaborate as ten thousand shards of ice coming together to coat the ground, and every flat surface, in a perfect sheet, or a raging bonfire erupting upwards in a mushroom cloud, or that for a moment every flower, tree, and plant in the area suddenly bursts into venomous bloom. It's unbridled power from inside the Exalt erupting outwards in displays that are blatantly unnatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have any real problem with this take on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T03:27:46-08:00","id":81499,"title":"","content":"This... Is exactly what I'd like to see more of. Air Aspects will have raging wind storms, Water Aspects torrential downpours, Fire Aspects will cause the temperature to spike to &quot;uncomfortably hot&quot;, Earth Aspects cause low-magnitude earthquakes, and Wood Aspects will see weeds growing out of control all over the place. None of these will actually have any mechanical effect barring stunts and thematics... Unless you invest in Dragon-Seared Battlefield or Dragon Vortex Attack, at which point shit goes down.<br /> <br /> Also, some ideas of how Celestials compare;<br /> Solars - Archangels. A totemic Solar Anima makes it blatantly clear that you are dealing with one Chosen by the Highest of Holies; to oppose one is to be Damned, for their Word is Law - to aid them is to be Blessed, for their Will is Divine.<br /> Abyssals/Infernals - As with Solars, except Dead-Thing-That-Should-Not-Be and Corrupt-Abomination-From-The-Depths-Of-Hell, respectively.<br /> Lunars - The Wild Hunt. No matter whether it is a raging Beast, a Wolf in sheep's clothing, or a Monster in the shadows, a Predator stands before you, a Hunter, and you can only pray you're not its prey. You feel the animal instincts surge to the fore, fight or flight, submit or die.<br /> Sidereals - Tricky, since their animas are by far the most subtle. I imagine that it just gives an overwhelming sensation of Destiny, almost like an out-of-body experience. You just <i>know</i> that This, Right Here, is a Key Part of The Big Plan. Or, far worse, Not Part Of The Plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T05:06:43-08:00","id":81522,"title":"","content":"God damn double-post. &quot;Error&quot; my ass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":578,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","user":"Lord Sia","date":". 03-01-2014, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T05:43:03-08:00","id":81534,"title":"","content":"I always wonder what Water-Aspected look like on land, does water just start to leak from everywhere or the sky begin to rain ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 02-28-2014, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T06:43:39-08:00","id":81562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always wonder what Water-Aspected look like on land, does water just start to leak from everywhere or the sky begin to rain ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to envision it as your essence flowing out from you, everything getting slick and the very air getting heavy, things start feeling heavy as if everyone was underwater...even the air slightly ripples with your movements as if everything has moved below the ocean, and your essence fueling phantom phenomena of deapsea dragons and perhaps other aquatic creatures at the totemic level.<br /> <br /> And of course, in battle, that flowing movement might start feeling like crashing waves as the essence bursts out in waves, attacking causing foam to form in the air, and even bystanders can feel the blows wash over them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":697,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","user":"Arteliex","date":". 02-28-2014, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T06:52:26-08:00","id":81570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/76114-storms-and-the-dragon-blooded?p=81534#post81534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always wonder what Water-Aspected look like on land, does water just start to leak from everywhere or the sky begin to rain ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that there's no obligation for water anima to be actual <b>water</b>, so you can just get the usual array of light effects in fashionable black. If you particularly like real water then ground-clinging fog, water drawn up from the water table into spontaneous puddles, and enforced condensation are all options. When the sun beats down mercilessly outside but water is beading on the window, you know a water aspect is near. <br /> <br /> I tend to avoid rain because of the general association of weather with the sky and the Air element. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T11:33:20-08:00","id":81694,"title":"","content":"I imagine Moist from Dr. Horrible's Sing-a-Long Blog...<br /> <br /> But I think it's totally thematic for a DB showdown to result in cosmetic cinematic effects. Like the thunderstorms that happen in the <i>Highlander</i> when Immortals fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}